       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Ben Pennell",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" data-account-id=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" accountid=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Danny Bernstein</a> I'm not quite sure what the expected outcome for this ticket is. Do we want `Want-Digest: sha-256` to produce `Digest: sha256=blahblahlblah`?</p>\n\n<p>\"sha-256\" appears to be the algorithm name expected by internal java libraries, so we would have to do some translation on the way out. I don't see any reason we can't retain the - in the urn specification, and my instinct would be to keep the keys matching on the input and output, but I don't feel strongly if there is reason to change it.</p>\n\n<p>As a bonus, there is an existing test that explicitly expects `sha256` to fail when requesting digests:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/kernel/modeshape/FedoraBinaryImplIT.java#L389\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/kernel/modeshape/FedoraBinaryImplIT.java#L389</a></p>",
     "created": "21/Sep/18 11:33 AM",
